### User Profile API Tests
### For use with VS Code REST Client extension or similar tools

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000
@email = testprofile@example.com
@userName = profileuser
@password = TestPass123!
@accessToken = YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE

### Setup: Register a new user
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "{{userName}}",
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "firstName": "Profile",
  "lastName": "Tester",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Expected Response:
### {
###   "message": "Registration successful! Please check your email to verify your account.",
###   "email": "testprofile@example.com",
###   "requiresEmailVerification": true
### }

###

### Setup: Verify email (replace TOKEN_FROM_EMAIL with actual token)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/verify-email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "token": "TOKEN_FROM_EMAIL"
}

###

### Setup: Login to get access token
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "rememberMe": false
}

### Expected Response:
### {
###   "accessToken": "jwt_token...",
###   "refreshToken": "refresh_token...",
###   "tokenType": "Bearer",
###   "expiresIn": 3600,
###   "userId": "...",
###   "userName": "profileuser",
###   "email": "testprofile@example.com",
###   "role": "User"
### }
### 
### IMPORTANT: Copy the accessToken from the response and replace YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE above

###

### 1. GET /api/users/profile - Get current user profile
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Expected Response (200 OK):
### {
###   "id": "user-guid",
###   "userName": "profileuser",
###   "email": "testprofile@example.com",
###   "emailConfirmed": true,
###   "firstName": "Profile",
###   "lastName": "Tester",
###   "phoneNumber": null,
###   "role": "User",
###   "isActive": true,
###   "createdAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z",
###   "updatedAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z",
###   "lastLoginAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z"
### }

###

### 2. GET /api/users/profile - Without authentication (should fail)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/profile
Accept: application/json

### Expected Response (401 Unauthorized)

###

### 3. PUT /api/users/profile - Update user profile
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/users/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Updated",
  "lastName": "Profile",
  "email": "testprofile@example.com",
  "phoneNumber": "+1234567890"
}

### Expected Response (200 OK):
### {
###   "id": "user-guid",
###   "userName": "profileuser",
###   "email": "testprofile@example.com",
###   "emailConfirmed": true,
###   "firstName": "Updated",
###   "lastName": "Profile",
###   "phoneNumber": "+1234567890",
###   "role": "User",
###   "isActive": true,
###   "createdAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z",
###   "updatedAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:01Z",
###   "lastLoginAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z"
### }

###

### 4. PUT /api/users/profile - Update with new email (requires verification)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/users/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Updated",
  "lastName": "Profile",
  "email": "newemail@example.com",
  "phoneNumber": "+1234567890"
}

### Expected Response (200 OK):
### Note: emailConfirmed will be false since email changed
### {
###   "id": "user-guid",
###   "userName": "profileuser",
###   "email": "newemail@example.com",
###   "emailConfirmed": false,
###   "firstName": "Updated",
###   "lastName": "Profile",
###   "phoneNumber": "+1234567890",
###   "role": "User",
###   "isActive": true,
###   "createdAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z",
###   "updatedAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:01Z",
###   "lastLoginAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z"
### }

###

### 5. PUT /api/users/profile - Invalid data (missing required fields)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/users/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "",
  "lastName": "Profile",
  "email": "invalid-email"
}

### Expected Response (400 Bad Request):
### Validation errors

###

### 6. PUT /api/users/change-password - Change password with valid credentials
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/users/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "{{password}}",
  "newPassword": "NewPass123!",
  "confirmPassword": "NewPass123!"
}

### Expected Response (200 OK):
### {
###   "message": "Password changed successfully"
### }

###

### 7. PUT /api/users/change-password - Invalid current password
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/users/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "WrongPassword123!",
  "newPassword": "NewPass123!",
  "confirmPassword": "NewPass123!"
}

### Expected Response (400 Bad Request):
### {
###   "message": "Current password is incorrect"
### }

###

### 8. PUT /api/users/change-password - Passwords don't match
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/users/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "{{password}}",
  "newPassword": "NewPass123!",
  "confirmPassword": "DifferentPass123!"
}

### Expected Response (400 Bad Request):
### Validation errors

###

### 9. PUT /api/users/change-password - Weak password
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/users/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "{{password}}",
  "newPassword": "weak",
  "confirmPassword": "weak"
}

### Expected Response (400 Bad Request):
### Password validation errors

###

### 10. DELETE /api/users/account - Delete user account (soft delete)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/users/account
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Expected Response (200 OK):
### {
###   "message": "Account has been deleted successfully"
### }
### 
### Note: This is a soft delete. The account will be marked as inactive
### but data is preserved for integrity

###

### 11. DELETE /api/users/account - Without authentication (should fail)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/users/account

### Expected Response (401 Unauthorized)

###

### 12. Verify account is inactive after deletion (should fail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "rememberMe": false
}

### Expected Response (401 Unauthorized):
### {
###   "message": "Account is not active"
### }

###
